led, since if it's called at a different place than the `init_input_device()` then might it be possible to inadvertently leak the old input device?\r\n> \r\n> I'm also concerned given the description that it's an AI generated pull request, since this would mean there is no human who understands how the rewritten code works well enough to reply to my review comments. I hope I didn't waste my time reviewing this.\r\n\r\nDamn bro i thought you was just gonna bash the code changes lol and just left hahah my bad i apologize.\r\nYes I do incorporate \"AI\" for transforming commit messages and dev notes to a PR description. I try to maximize my workflow this way :D (sometimes oopsies happen tho heheh)\r\n\r\nWeekend is over now sadly, we can hop in a call next weekend where I can go through my intentions with you if that is something of your preference else I will write together in text.\r\n\r\nI also learned recently that there seems to be other major audio reworks in progress so I will  have to crosscheck their ideas and potential implementations against my potential changes. \r\n\r\nIf they collide then this PR and fix might be void anyway. I apologize for misinterpreting your initial comment.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3124552566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]